<title>RUSSIA: Russian international airport charges in March.</title>
<headline>Russian international airport charges in March.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current charges of 11 international Russian regional airports in roubles for March, comprising landing fees (L), maintenance fees (M), passenger charges (P), fuel cost per tonne (F) and cost for meteorological data (W):</p>
<p>			  L	     M	 P	F	    W</p>
<p> Irkutsk	   1,651,121   340,000  59,488  1,429,876 345,524</p>
<p> Khabarovsk	1,237,550   651,800  42,650  1,598,467 405,333</p>
<p> Krasnoyarsk     1,890,000   727,544  53,300  1,499,429 280,000</p>
<p> Kazan	     1,983,840   422,330  44,160  1,322,000 305,000</p>
<p> Novosibirsk	 960,000   295,000  43,000  1,371,500 498,070</p>
<p> Omsk		1,319,618   180,263  28,992  1,302,006 262,710</p>
<p> Samara	    1,489,000   365,000  37,730  1,160,000  n/a</p>
<p> St Petersburg   1,547,200   502,841  52,672  1,343,333 530,000</p>
<p> Vladivostok     2,278,352 1,080,000  61,009  1,716,000  n/a</p>
<p> Yakutsk	   4,331,600 1,824,954  88,790  3,120,997 290,769</p>
<p> Yekaterinburg   2,184,868   322,178  46,052  1,243,500 332,582</p>
<p>Charges do not include value-added tax.</p>
<p>Landing and maintenance rates are quoted for Yakovlev Yak-40 passenger jets. They should be multiplied by the following coefficients for other passenger aircraft:</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-62     8.4		A-310	 7.8</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-96    10.6		Boeing 727  4.8</p>
<p>    Antonov  An-124   32.9		Boeing 737  2.6</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-154M    8.0		Boeing 747 16.0</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-204     6.0		Boeing 757  6.9</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-134     2.2		Boeing 767  8.2</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-154M    8.0		DC-10	11.0</p>
<p>Airport officials declined to say what dollar exchange rates would be used. The official exchange rate for the dollar on Thursday was 5,700 roubles.</p>
<p>--Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
